From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32, explorer: jump lists

ICustomDestinationList, IApplicationDestinations and
IApplicationDocumentLists were E_NOTIMPL stubs, and there was no
EnumerableObjectCollection at all -- the object programs build their
jump list categories and tasks in, so their CoCreateInstance failed.
SHAddToRecentDocs knew only paths and ID lists, and clearing it left the
Recent folder's shortcuts.

- EnumerableObjectCollection (IObjectCollection, IObjectArray).
- ICustomDestinationList: SetAppID, BeginList (the slots the taskbar
  shows, and what the user removed), AppendCategory (documents as shell
  items and links; a removed one is E_ACCESSDENIED), AppendKnownCategory
  (Recent, Frequent), AddUserTasks (links, with separators), CommitList,
  AbortList, DeleteList, GetRemovedDestinations; calls out of order are
  E_UNEXPECTED. A committed list is kept per AppUserModelID (the explicit
  one, else the program's path) under the Recent folder, in a format of
  our own.
- SHAddToRecentDocs takes SHARD_APPIDINFO, SHARD_APPIDINFOIDLIST,
  SHARD_LINK, SHARD_APPIDINFOLINK and SHARD_SHELLITEM, and puts the
  document on its program's list too (with its use count), unless
  NoRecentDocsHistory is set. Clearing it deletes the Recent shortcuts and
  the programs' document lists.
- IApplicationDocumentLists.GetList gives a program's documents most
  recent or most used first; IApplicationDestinations removes one or all.
- The taskbar shows a program's jump list at the top of its button's
  menu (and a pinned program's): the categories, Recent/Frequent where
  the program asked for them -- or its recent documents when it has no
  list of its own -- and its tasks; choosing a task runs it, a document
  opens in the program.

Wine's shell32 shelllink, shlfolder and shellole tests: as before.

Gate: test/jumplist-gate.sh (Xvfb, test/jumplist-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_COMMIT_NOTHING (shell32/jumplist.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_APP_RECENT (shell32/shellord.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_JUMP_MENU
(explorer/systray.c).
---
--- a/dlls/shell32/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/shell32/Makefile.in
@@ -102,4 +102,5 @@ SOURCES = \
 	shpolicy.c \
 	systray.c \
 	vdesktopmgr.c \
-	zipfolder.c
+	zipfolder.c \
+	jumplist.c
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/shell32/jumplist.c
@@ -0,0 +1,1522 @@
